# Art assets (retro style: off-white on near-black, square pixels). Canvas 800x500, drawn at 1x, nearest-neighbour scaling.

Regenerate with `python3 tools/gen_assets.py`. Paths match game-developer's `docs/assets.md` (artist#2).

## `assets/palette.css`
`:root` vars: `--bg #101010`, `--fg #f0f0f0`, `--accent #ffd23f` (winner text / highlights), `--dim #8a8a8a` (hints), `--font-family` (Courier New monospace stack; no font file shipped).

## Images (`assets/img/`, PNG RGBA)
- `logo.png` 456x168 — "PONG" title logo, transparent, off-white.
- `paddle.png` 12x80 — both paddles.
- `ball.png` 12x12 — ball.
- `centerline.png` 4x24 — tile vertically down the centre (opaque top 12px, transparent bottom 12px).

## Audio (`assets/audio/`, mono 16-bit PCM WAV, 22050 Hz, square-wave beeps)
- `paddle.wav` 0.07s — ball hits paddle (480 Hz).
- `wall.wav` 0.06s — ball hits top/bottom wall (240 Hz).
- `score.wav` 0.38s — point scored (descending).
- `win.wav` 0.76s — player wins match (ascending arpeggio).
- `lose.wav` 1.04s — computer wins match (descending).
Audio needs a user gesture (the key press that starts the game).
